# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: neutralize the only blocker before committing attackers.
# Forcing: two Coursers deal exactly six; the Wall blocks enough damage to prevent the one-turn win.
# AI behavior: the blocker is already on the field and the opponent has no hand decisions.
# Failure modes: WIN means both attacks connected after removal; LOSE means the blocker stopped lethal or the turn expired; TIMEOUT means play stopped.
# Card roles: Pacifism disables the Wall; two Coursers provide exact lethal; Plains pay the cost; the Wall blocks an unprepared attack; library lands prevent an empty draw.
# Protocol path: cast action, permanent target, stack resolution, declare attackers, combat damage, terminal win.
